# Muon on the 2020 baseline (baseline.bux: gpt3_2020.bux at every rung), its model
# unchanged: does Muon's gain on the factorial's candidate (ideas_opt.bux's muon,
# -2.2% at d512) hold on older architectures? A training option, not architecture.
# Muon (Jordan et al., 2024) for the matrices in the blocks, at Moonlight's update
# RMS of 0.2, so AdamW's learning rate suits it; AdamW at the baseline's 2e-3 for the
# rest: the embedding, the head, the norms and the biases.
use gpt3_2020
use timeline_code
use rungs

optimizer = muon(lr=2e-3, weight_decay=0.1, adam=adamw(lr=2e-3, weight_decay=0.1))
